.SS "static void initialize_window (\fBt_data\fP * data, char * argv[])\fC [static]\fP"

.PP
Initializes the MLX42 rendering environment\&. This function sets up the environment for rendering fractals by:
.IP "\(bu" 2
Creating an MLX42 window with thee given title\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Allocating an image buffer for rendering\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Setting initial offsets and zoom level for the fractal\&.
.PP
.PP
If Julia set parameters (\fCc[COMPLEX_RE]\fP or \fCc[COMPLEX_IM]\fP) are outside the range [-2\&.0, 2\&.0], it issues a warning about potential visual effects\&. The function terminates the program in case of initialization failures\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdata\fP Pointer to the data structure containing fractal information, offsets, zoom, and MLX42 resources\&. 
.br
\fIargv\fP Array of argument strings, where argv[1] is used as the window title\&. 
.RE
.PP

