.SS "static void validate_arguments (int argc, char * argv[])\fC [static]\fP"

.PP
Validates the command-line arguments for fractal rendering\&. This function checks that the user has specified a valid fractal type and the correct parameters\&. The supported fractals and their requirements are:
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fCmandelbrot\fP: No additional arguments\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fCjulia\fP: Requires exactly two valid numbers representing the real and imaginary part of the parameter\&.
.PP
.PP
If the arguments are invalid, the function calls \fC\fBexit_with_error()\fP\fP to display an appropiate error message and terminate the program\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIargc\fP Number of command-line arguments passed to the program\&. 
.br
\fIargv\fP Array of command-line argument strings\&. 
.RE
.PP

